`run develop` over a plan's directory resolves its `index.md`, records the plan's planned
item, launches `core.run.command` with the session id and the prompt naming the absolute plan
path, `core.run.env` set and stdin empty, and writes the outcome; the child's output lands in
the log only.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/config.yaml --
macro_stubs:
  core.macros.date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S: "20261015-120000"
  core.macros.date +%Y-%m-%d %H:%M: "2026-10-15 12:00"
core:
  run:
    command:
      - sh
      - -c
      - |
        printf 'arg: %s\n' "$@"
        echo "env: $CLAUDE_CODE_PRINT_BG_WAIT_CEILING_MS"
        if read -r line; then echo "stdin: data"; else echo "stdin: empty"; fi
        exit 0
      - fake
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/p1/index.md --
---
title: P1
status: ready-for-dev
---
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/open-items/OI-0001.md --
---
id: OI-0001
title: "Gap OI-0001"
status: planned
direction: clarify
record: null
source: manual
plan: plans/p1/index.md
created_at: 2026-10-01
closed_at: null
reason: null
---

# Gap OI-0001
